I</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAIZUMI KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOIKE ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHATA TAKAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGISHI KIYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAIZUMI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOIKE, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHATA, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGISHI, KIYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A strainer integrated flowmeter (201) which comprises a strainer section (203) including a housing (202) formed with a flow passage (207), a filter member (209) and a filter member insertion cylinder (210), and a flowmeter section (204) including the housing (202) formed with a flow passage (208) and a flow sensor (226). The housing (202) for the strainer section (203) and flowmeter section (204) is shared therebetween and integrated, with the flowmeter section (204) disposed downstream the strainer section. The housing (202) has an exhaust hole (215) connected to the flow passage (207). This arrangement makes it difficult for foreign matter to enter the flowmeter and prevents air bubbles from remaining in the flow passage, thus making it possible to measure the flow rate of a fluid flowing through a pipeline accurately for a long time.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un débitmètre intégré à grille (201) comprenant une grille (203), et présentant un logement (202) formé par un passage d'écoulement (207), un filtre (209) et un cylindre d'introduction de filtre (210), un débitmètre (204) comprenant le logement (202) formé par le passage d'écoulement (208) et un détecteur de débit (226). Ce logement (202) est intégré et partagé entre la grille (203) et le débitmètre (204), le débitmètre (204) étant disposé en aval de la grille. De plus, ce logement (202) est pourvu d'un trou d'échappement (215) relié au passage d'écoulement (207). En outre, ce dispositif ne permet pas aux matières étrangères de pénétrer le débitmètre et empêche les bulles d'air de rester dans le passage d'écoulement, permettant ainsi de mesurer avec précision le débit d'un fluide s'écoulant à travers un pipeline pendant longtemps.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>